      "type": "token",
      "content": "**Quick read:** Apple’s fundamentals are strong, but its valuation is demanding and sentiment is positive but divided.\n\n| Area | Read |\n|---|---|\n| Fundamentals | Fiscal third-quarter revenue was **$109,417,000,000**, up **16%** year over year, while net income was **$29,789,000,000** and net margin was **27%**. Apple said tariff refunds boosted gross margin and earnings, so part of the quarter’s strength was non-recurring. |\n| Valuation | As of **2026-09-10**, AAPL traded at **$326.57**, with a market capitalization of **$4,796,449,848,920** and a P/E ratio of **37.41x**. That is a premium valuation and leaves less room for execution disappointments. |\n| Sentiment | Analyst sentiment was a mixed-positive “Moderate Buy”: **22** Buy, **12** Hold and **4** Sell ratings, with an average target of **$330.61**. The target sits only slightly above the current share price, while published concerns center on valuation and AI execution. |\n\n**Bottom line:** Apple is delivering healthy growth and high profitability, but the share price already reflects substantial optimism. This is an informational snapshot, not investment advice."
